{"operations":[{"content":"\"\"\"money: cent rounding for ledgers.\"\"\"\n\n\ndef round_cents(amount):\n    \"\"\"Round a decimal amount to cents, halves away from zero.\"\"\"\n    # Multiply by 100 to shift cents, then round halves away from zero\n    # Python's built-in round uses round half to even, so implement manually\n    sign = 1 if amount >= 0 else -1\n    shifted = abs(amount) * 100\n    # Add 0.5 to shift halves away from zero, then floor\n    shifted_rounded = int(shifted + 0.5)\n    return sign * shifted_rounded / 100\n","expected_sha256":"fa816984cb1f791630c850f452d214933dceee46a979c2276da8800a2c0570db","kind":"modify","path":"src/money.py"}],"rationale":"Replaced built-in round with manual rounding that rounds halves away from zero as required, preserving public API and usage in ledger.total."}